Z||000000||GREENDANO||01-09-2000||03:20 PM||||Hey everybody,<BR>  Got a digital camera yesterday.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Here's a picture of my brakes on my F40 kit.  What you're looking at is the rear knuckle with a Grand Am caliper and rotor.  I chamfered the patern into the face of the rotor to make them look crossdrilled.  <BR>  This was a heck of a lot cheaper than buying actual crossdrilled rotors.  <BR>  Dan-O<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Crossdrilled.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Harry||01-09-2000||03:28 PM||||How did you drill them (and still maintain balance) with a press?||||reg||14
Z||000002||GREENDANO||01-09-2000||03:32 PM||||You are correct, I drilled them on my drill press with a pattern I made.  The difference in balance is negligiable.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||3
Z||000003||Monkeyman||01-09-2000||05:36 PM||||That looks great!  Aren't digicams just about the neatest thing since sliced bread?!  And did you know that the red paint will only give you an extra 5hp?  If you had used yellow paint you could have gotten almost 15hp! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||GREENDANO||01-09-2000||05:54 PM||||My GT that I traded did have yellow rotors and calipers.  Now it all makes sense.....<BR>  Now adding 5 HP to the brakes, does that make it stop beter?  Or does it slow the car's top speed because of the power?<BR>  Thanks for the compliment.  Yeah, I do like having the camera on hand.  I like the instant gratification.  I want my pictures NOW.  Last roll of film I developed about two weeks ago had spring and summer pictures on the same roll.  <BR>  Dan-O||||reg||5
